      "note": "Played on whatever riff the theme drew, by its runs, never its notes, each drawn among its variants by weight: rest (once a phrase) — when the drums get busy at a phrase's end (a pickup, a fill) the run held there ends on the variant's step of the last bar and the line rests to the next phrase, which enters fresh; glide (once a phrase) — when the drums open the end the run held there rises the variant's semitones from its step to the phrase's end, across the gap. halfTime (once a track): the sentence the line plays in a half-time phrase, two bars on the riff's own voice and register — a long travel up a fifth into the middle backbeat and a short falling answer; a note held into a third and answered from the fifth; one long note that falls a tone at its end."
